 many gigabytes of data, but the system does not need to load the complete file into memory. Instead, the file is processed using smaller buffers. This makes the storage system more memory efficient and allows it to work with files that are much larger than the available RAM.

ChunkVault also focuses on performance. Multiple chunks can eventually be processed in parallel using multiple worker threads. Synchronization mechanisms such as mutexes and locks can be used to protect shared resources. Database transactions can be used to maintain consistency when multiple operations occur at the same time.

The ultimate goal of ChunkVault is to provide reliable, scalable, and fault-tolerant file storage using chunking, replication, metadata management, database support, concurrency, failure detection, and recovery mechanisms.

ChunkVault is a practical implementation of concepts from operating systems and database management systems. It demonstrates how file storage can be designed to handle large data, storage failures, concurrent operations, and data recovery while maintaining consistency and reliability.